---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import AdRow from '../components/AdRow.astro';
---
<Layout title="How Local Buzz ATX works" current="About">
  <section class="page prose">
    <h2>How Local Buzz ATX works</h2>
    <p>Local Buzz ATX collects headlines from Austin-area news organizations in one place, adds context with a short "Why should I care?" line, and links you straight to the original reporting.</p>
    <h3>Where the stories come from</h3>
    <p>Each outlet publishes a public feed of its headlines. We show the headline, a short blurb and the outlet's own photo, and every click goes to the outlet's site. We do not copy full articles.</p>
    <h3>What the AI does</h3>
    <p>Some short lines, such as "Why should I care?" and the "What matters today" headlines, are written with the help of an AI tool. It only uses the headline and blurb the outlet published, and it is told not to add facts. If there is no clear Austin angle, it says so. Always check the original story for the full picture.</p>
    <h3>Guides</h3>
    <p>Our <a href="/guides">guides</a> are plain-English how-tos for Travis and Williamson counties. They are put together from official city, county and agency sources. Each one lists its sources and the date it was last checked. If you see a mistake, see <a href="/corrections">Corrections</a>.</p>
    <h3>Columns</h3>
    <p>Caleb (tech and cybersecurity) and Tori (culture and entertainment) are pen names for our columnists. Their pieces are opinion and commentary, and they say so. <a href="/mind-the-marbles">Mind the Marbles</a> is a recurring humor and observation column.</p>
    <h3>Community resources</h3>
    <p>We keep a <a href="/resources">list of local organizations</a> that help readers. They are not news sources and do not pay to be listed.</p>
    <h3>OMG!</h3>
    <p>OMG! is our humor column. The jokes are AI-assisted and reviewed by a person, aimed at the situation, not at anyone in particular. They are humor and opinion, not news.
    <AdRow />
  </section>
</Layout>
